==English==
===Pronunciation===
*Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-ʌfɪn|-ʌfɪn]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|UK}} a type of [[flattish]] bun, usually cut in two [[horizontally]], [[toast]]ed and spread with butter, etc, before being eaten
# {{context|especially US}} A type of rich [[individual]] cake containing [[chocolate chip]]s, [[blueberry|blueberries]] or some other flavouring.
# {{context|computing}} a [[mechanism]] used in the [[w:Java Network Launching Protocol|Java Network Launching Protocol]] [[analogous]] to the [[cookie]] mechanism and which permits a program running in a [[browser]] to perform operations on a client machine
# {{context|slang}} a term of endearment<!--, e.g. "nuffin' muffin"-->
# {{context|sexual slang}} a [[vulva]]
# {{context|baseball|slang}} a less [[talented]] player
# {{context|slang}} a charming, attractive young man

====Quotations====
'''computing term'''
*'''2001''': The name/value pairs provided by the PersistenceService are similar to browser cookies. The Java Web Start implementation honors this legacy by naming the pairs "'''muffins'''." &mdash; ''JNLP and Java Web Start'', Sun Developer Network, Technical Articles and Tips, 30 May 2001.
'''the vulva'''
*'''1989''': I wanna be stuffin' Martha's '''muffin'''!!!, &mdash; Mojo Nixon and Skid Roper ''Stuffin' Martha's Muffin''.

